Package: indi-stable-core
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs (= ${binary:Version})
Description: INDI core library and server (stable upstream release, private prefix)
 INDI (Instrument-Neutral Distributed Interface) is a distributed control
 protocol for astronomical instrumentation. This package provides indiserver
 and the bundled device drivers, built from an upstream stable release tag.
 .
 It installs into a private prefix (/opt/indi-stable) and registers
 indiserver-stable through update-alternatives, so it coexists with a
 distribution-provided INDI rather than replacing it. Nothing this package
 installs overwrites a file owned by another package -- notably it does not
 conflict with indi-bin, which kstars depends on.
 .
 This is an unofficial third-party build. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by the INDI project.

Package: indi-stable-core-libs
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Shared libraries for indi-stable-core
 The INDI client, driver and alignment shared libraries, installed under
 /opt/indi-stable/lib.
 .
 These deliberately do NOT use the standard library search path. Consumers
 find them through RPATH instead, so they can never shadow a distribution
 INDI: this project ships stable releases just as the distribution does, so
 both carry libindiclient.so.2 and SONAME alone would not keep them apart.
 .
 The package is therefore not named liblindiclient2 or similar. Debian's
 lib<name><soversion> convention exists for libraries in the public linker
 path that other packages link against; these are private to indi-stable.

Package: indi-stable-core-dev
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Development files for indi-stable-core
 Headers, static libraries and pkg-config metadata for building against
 indi-stable-core.
 .
 Headers install to /opt/indi-stable/include, NOT /usr/include/libindi. That
 is deliberate and load-bearing: headers are not SONAME-versioned, and
 /usr/include precedes any private path in the default compiler search
 order, so a distribution libindi-dev left installed would silently win and
 the build would quietly use the wrong INDI.
 .
 Build against this package with:
   PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/opt/indi-stable/lib/pkgconfig \
     pkg-config --cflags --libs libindi
